Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 11:16:36 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] fix(chat): enforce chat membership before reading
 messages or read receipts
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

GET /api/chat/:id/messages and POST /api/chat/:id/read trusted only the chatId
from the URL and never checked whether the caller was a participant, so any
authenticated user could read private conversations by enumerating chat ids
(IDOR / broken access control, medium-high).

- getChatMessages(userId, chatId, ...) now verifies the caller is a chat
  participant (404 if the chat does not exist, 403 if not a member) before
  querying messages.
- markAsRead now verifies membership via chatParticipant before creating read
  receipts.
- chat.controller passes req.user.userId into both.

Tests: server/src/services/chat.service.test.ts - non-participant read is
rejected and no messages are fetched; unknown chat 404s; participant reads
work; non-participant read receipts rejected; participant path works.

Run: cd server && npx jest src/services/chat.service.test.ts

